    "physical_description": "Skirt cloth (<i>kain panjang</i>) of cotton batik. Batik on a cotton mill cloth with a cream ground and an overall pattern of mythological birds amongst flowering vines and tendrils, in maroon and deep maroon. The pattern is framed with a single line 0.5 inch thick within the outer edge of cloth.",
    "summary": "This batik skirt cloth or <i>kain panjang</i> is of cotton mill cloth and has a cream ground with an overall pattern of mythological birds among flowering vines and tendrils. It was made in Cirebon on the north coast of Java in the late 19th century.",
